1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,130
May 2010. Jacksonville, Florida.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,350
A programmer named Laszlo Hanyecz is hungry.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,480
He posts on a bitcoin forum:
"I will pay ten thousand bitcoins for two pizzas."

4
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:15,360
Someone takes the deal.
Two large pizzas arrive at his door.

5
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:19,500
Back then, those ten thousand bitcoins
were worth about forty dollars.

6
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:22,080
But the price of bitcoin kept climbing.

7
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:32,350
In 2013, those pizzas were worth seven million dollars.
In 2017, $190 million. In 2021, almost $700 million.

8
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,000
Today, those two pizzas are worth
over a billion dollars.

9
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:42,760
The most expensive dinner in history. Every May 22nd,
the crypto world celebrates Bitcoin Pizza Day.
